# National Auto Spares — counter application, PRODUCTION template
# ================================================================
#
# Copy to `.env.production` for a local reproduction of the Vercel bundle
# (`npm run build -- --mode production`). `.env.production` is git-ignored; this file is
# committed and holds PLACEHOLDERS ONLY.
#
# ⚠️ ANYTHING VITE_-PREFIXED IS COMPILED INTO A PUBLICLY READABLE BUNDLE.
#
# There is no such thing as a secret in this repository (NFR-SEC-012). No database URL,
# no JWT signing key, no password or IP pepper, no storage credential, no Neon connection
# string — not even in a file called `.env.production`. `tests/structural/rules.test.ts`
# fails the build if any of those strings appears anywhere in `src/`, and `gitleaks` runs
# on every push.
#
# WHAT VERCEL ACTUALLY USES
# -------------------------
# Not this file. Vercel supplies `VITE_API_BASE_URL` from Project → Settings →
# Environment Variables at build time, and an inline `VITE_`-prefixed variable takes
# precedence over every `.env*` file in Vite. This template exists so the intended value
# is recorded somewhere reviewable and so a local production build is reproducible.
#
# Full Vercel configuration: `docs/VERCEL-ENVIRONMENT-VARIABLES.md`.
#
# ONLY FOUR VARIABLES ARE PERMITTED
# ---------------------------------
# `src/vite-env.d.ts` declares them and a structural test asserts no fifth is referenced.
# Of the four, exactly one is read by the application today — `VITE_API_BASE_URL`, in
# `src/api/client.ts`. The other three are allow-listed seams with no reader in `src/`;
# setting them changes nothing. They are listed, commented, so nobody has to grep to find
# that out.


# --- the API base URL --------------------------------------------------------
#
# Read at BUILD time, baked into the bundle. Changing it needs a redeploy, not a restart.
#
# It must include the `/api/v1` path: `client.ts` appends endpoint paths directly to it
# and strips only a trailing slash.
#
# TWO VALID SHAPES, and the choice is a topology decision made once —
# `../bmbackend/docs/PRODUCTION-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md §10` has the comparison:
#
#  A. ABSOLUTE — the browser talks to Railway directly.
#     VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.your-domain.com/api/v1
#
#     Needs: `BM_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` on Railway to list this site's origin, and the
#     CSP's `connect-src` to permit this origin — which `vite.config.ts` appends
#     automatically from this very variable, so there is nothing to keep in sync.
#
#     ⚠️ If the two hosts are on different *provider* domains (`*.vercel.app` talking to
#     `*.up.railway.app`) the refresh cookie is `SameSite`-blocked and sessions die 15
#     minutes after every login. Either use two subdomains of one owned domain, or set
#     `BM_REFRESH_COOKIE_SAMESITE=none` on Railway. This is the single most likely way
#     for this deployment to look fine and then fail at the counter.
#
#  B. RELATIVE — Vercel proxies `/api/*` through to Railway via a `vercel.json` rewrite.
#     VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
#
#     Needs: the rewrite in `vercel.json`. Needs NO CORS entry, NO CSP widening and NO
#     cookie change, because the browser only ever sees one origin. Costs an extra network
#     hop, and Vercel's proxy body-size and duration limits then apply to the 10 MB import
#     upload and the 30-second finalisation.
#
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://REPLACE-WITH-YOUR-API-HOST/api/v1


# --- allow-listed, but read by nothing in src/ -------------------------------
#
# Declared in `src/vite-env.d.ts` and permitted by the structural test. Left commented
# because setting them has no effect today, and a variable that looks configured but
# changes nothing is worse than an absent one.
#
# `VITE_APP_VERSION` — intended as a build stamp. The release identifier the running
#   system actually reports comes from the backend: `BM_RELEASE` → `GET /api/v1/meta`.
# VITE_APP_VERSION=
#
# `VITE_SENTRY_DSN` — no Sentry SDK is installed in `package.json`.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
#
# `VITE_ENABLE_DEVTOOLS` — no reader in `src/`. Must never be set in production anyway.
# VITE_ENABLE_DEVTOOLS=
